WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
The Jewish People

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:11.000
It's a fantastic, it's going to be the most interesting perasha so far.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:15.000
I don't know what is the most interesting, but it's a fabulous perasha.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:22.000
You remember when we left last time.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:29.000
Finally, Pharaoh breaks down and Pharaoh releases the Jewish people.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:37.000
Not as an act of goodwill, but under the pressure of the Almighty Lord.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.000
Alright?

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:39.000
Amen.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:44.640
And we assume that that's the end of the story.

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:48.440
The Jewish people leave Egypt.

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:53.480
And the drama, we imagine, it's already ended.

00:00:53.480 --> 00:01:00.500
But in point of fact, another chapter, the last chapter is going to come about.

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:05.860
And this last chapter is the most fantastic grandiose finale.

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:12.380
The whole thing is talking, whatever happened in Egypt is going to be kind of a prelude

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:14.380
to the ultimate miracle.

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:18.300
And we're going to see how the ultimate miracle operates.

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:25.400
It operates both into the world of the mind and the world of nature, but in a grandiose way.

00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:29.940
Now how it operates in the world of the mind?

00:01:30.660 --> 00:01:34.920
Because you're going to see that all of a sudden, even after everything that happened,

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:37.940
Pharaoh is going to be changing his mind.

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:44.260
And that that is going to be changing his mind is not his own mind that's changing his own self,

00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:55.140
but is rather the hand of the Lord entering inside Pharaoh, twisting his mind, forcing him in a way to follow the Jewish people,

00:01:55.780 --> 00:02:03.760
so to use him as a small pawn in the greatest of all miracles, the split of the Red Sea.

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:06.460
Now we're going to see how it's going to be.

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:16.060
and it came to pass at the moment when Pharaoh was sending the people

00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:24.340
yes and something interesting happened

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:32.260
now if you picture the map of Egypt in your mind you could imagine you see the

00:02:32.260 --> 00:02:38.440
Mediterranean, if you just go north to the Mediterranean, then you just follow to your

00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:45.040
right, yes? The coastline eventually in a couple of days you arrive to Israel. It's

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:52.060
the shortest and easiest way to travel. Follow the coastline. See? The Mediterranean coastline

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:57.820
up to Israel. You go straight into Israel. That is called in Hebrew,

00:02:57.820 --> 00:03:02.320
the way to go to the land of the Philistines.

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:15.800
But God did not conduct, did not direct the people through the land, through the path of the highway of the Philistine.

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:18.280
And God had a reason.

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:24.800
Because that would be too near to the Holy Land.

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:28.800
So what's wrong to be immediately in the Holy Land?

